    {
      "id": "claim_8a538ce5a51a468dbf7ee0f3df2032c3",
      "statement": "UniformRandomPlanner.selectSongs groups candidates by raw play count (playCounts[id] ?: 0) into ascending tiers — tier 0 = smallest-count group, tier 1 = next, remaining groups flattened as fallback — and fills the quota by tier priority with in-tier shuffling, never crossing into higher tiers while a lower tier has songs. Thresholds derive from the current distribution, so tiering survives when every song has been played past any fixed threshold, and equal counts degenerate to a single tier (pure shuffle). With the flag off it plain-shuffles.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://domain/src/main/java/cn/com/dcsgo/mihx/domain/playback/UniformRandomPlanner.kt#L9-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48593e99137f6795156b1b503666b89764c75f9c3135d0d03d67e488879439e6:"
