    {
      "id": "claim_9cac2a917e8b47219ef49de765a7229f",
      "statement": "startInfinitePlay keeps the current queue untouched: planInfiniteStart only records the queued playable song ids as the infinitePlayedSongIds coverage set, and an empty queue is legal (mode starts armed, waiting for refills). If the controller is already near the tail (remainingMediaItems() <= 5) it refills immediately, so the next track (natural end or system media keys) is a new song instead of a REPEAT_MODE_ALL wrap back to the old window's first item.",
